{"id": "EUVD-2026-102357", "enisaUuid": "59f90633-947b-388a-92eb-9ac3431db214", "description": "catdoc through 0.95 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the MULRK record handler of process_item() in src/xlsparse.c that allows attackers to read past the static rec buffer via a crafted end column. Attackers can supply a crafted .xls workbook or BIFF stream with a large endcol to xls2csv to disclose adjacent process memory as CSV cells or crash the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:54:23", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/catdoc-xls-mulrk-endcol-and-string-count-oob-read", "https://github.com/vbwagner/catdoc/blob/38a2807d22ce1a08bc39b94e9072a9f8f52cd86f/src/xlsparse.c#L314-L328", "https://github.com/vbwagner/catdoc", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/catdoc-through-0.95-out-of-bounds-read-in-xls2csv-mulrk-record-handler"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111126", "GHSA-gc5h-x8q8-5m4r"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "284030b6-66bd-38ef-8a98-3011bccbb70f", "product": {"name": "catdoc", "vendor": {"name": "catdoc"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.95"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fe7abd80-215a-33d6-b228-301085cfa613", "vendor": {"name": "catdoc"}}], "isExploited": false}